                <pb facs="0843" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Moose, James S./418: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-14T17:00:00-04:00">April 14, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>536. Personal for the Minister. For your information the President desires to
                    appoint Mr. James S. Moose, Jr. to act as Minister Resident to Saudi Arabia and
                    has instructed the Legation at Jidda to request Mr. Moose’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">agrément</hi>.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
